.\" ###### Setup ############################################################
.Dd October 17, 2026
.Dt gs\-glossytext 1
.Os gs\-glossytext
.\" ###### Name #############################################################
.Sh NAME
.Nm gs\-glossytext
.Nd applies the GIMP Script\-Fu \[dq]Glossy\[dq] filter on an image
.\" ###### Synopsis #########################################################
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm gs\-glossytext
.Ar output\_filename text
.br
.Op Fl F Ar font | Fl \-font\-name Ar font
.Op Fl S Ar size | Fl \-font\-size Ar size
.br
.Op Fl G Ar gradient | Fl \-blend\-gradient\-text Ar gradient
.br
.Op Fl g Ar on|off | Fl \-blend\-gradient\-text\-reverse Ar on|off
.br
.Op Fl L Ar gradient | Fl \-blend\-gradient\-outline Ar gradient
.br
.Op Fl l Ar on|off | Fl \-blend\-gradient\-outline\-reverse Ar on|off
.br
.Op Fl O Ar size | Fl \-outline\-size Ar size
.br
.Op Fl B Ar color | Fl \-background\-color Ar color
.br
.Op Fl I Ar pattern | Fl \-pattern\-text Ar pattern
.br
.Op Fl i Ar on|off | Fl \-use\-pattern\-text Ar on|off
.br
.Op Fl J Ar pattern | Fl \-pattern\-outline Ar pattern
.br
.Op Fl j Ar on|off | Fl \-use\-pattern\-outline Ar on|off
.br
.Op Fl R Ar pattern | Fl \-pattern\-overlay Ar pattern
.br
.Op Fl r Ar on|off | Fl \-use\-pattern\-overlay Ar on|off
.br
.Op Fl s Ar on|off | Fl \-use\-shadow Ar on|off
.br
.Op Fl X Ar offset | Fl \-shadow\-offset\-x Ar offset
.br
.Op Fl Y Ar offset | Fl \-shadow\-offset\-y Ar offset
.br
.Op Fl q | Fl \-quiet
.Op Fl w | Fl \-verbose
.Nm gs\-glossytext
.Op Fl h | Fl \-help
.Nm gs\-glossytext
.Op Fl v | Fl \-version
.\" ###### Description ######################################################
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm gs\-glossytext
runs GIMP and the GIMP Script\-Fu \[dq]Glossy Logo\[dq] script
(details:
.Lk https://docs.gimp.org/2.8/en/script\-fu\-glossy\-logo\-alpha.html "GIMP Script\-Fu Alpha to Logo Filters" )
to render a given text using a specific font.
The color gradients, patterns, font, and font size are configurable.
.\" ###### Arguments ########################################################
.Sh ARGUMENTS
The following arguments and options are available:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Ar output\_filename
The name for the output image to be written.
Any format supported by GIMP can be used.
The format will be detected by the provided file name extension (e.g. .jpeg, .png, .webp, .pdf, ...).
An existing output file will be overwritten.
.It Ar text
The text to be printed.
.It Fl F Ar font | Fl \-font\-name Ar font
Specifies the font and style to be used.
Font and style are space separated, e.g. \[dq]URW Gothic Book Oblique\[dq] for font \[dq]URW Gothic\[dq] in style \[dq]URW Gothic Book Oblique\[dq].
The available font/style combinations can be listed with
.Xr gs\-list\-fonts 1.
.It Fl S Ar size | Fl \-font\-size Ar size
Specifies the font size in pixels. Default: 50.
.It Fl G Ar gradient | Fl \-blend\-gradient\-text Ar gradient
Specifies the blend gradient for the text, e.g. \[dq]Golden\[dq].
The name must be a gradient in GIMP (.ggr file, usually in
.Pa /usr/share/gimp/*/gradients/
or
.Pa /usr/local/share/gimp/*/gradients/ ).
The available gradients can be listed with
.Xr gs\-list\-gradients 1.
Default: Golden.
.It Fl g Ar on|off | Fl \-blend\-gradient\-text\-reverse Ar on|off
Turns reversing the blend gradient for the text on or off. Default: off.
.It Fl L Ar gradient | Fl \-blend\-gradient\-outline Ar gradient
Specifies the blend gradient for the outline, e.g. \[dq]Golden\[dq].
The name must be a gradient in GIMP (.ggr file, usually in
.Pa /usr/share/gimp/*/gradients/
or
.Pa /usr/local/share/gimp/*/gradients/ ).
The available gradients can be listed with
.Xr gs\-list\-gradients 1.
Default: Golden.
.It Fl l Ar on|off | Fl \-blend\-gradient\-outline\-reverse Ar on|off
Turns reversing the blend gradient for the outline on or off. Default: off.
.It Fl O Ar size | Fl \-outline\-size Ar size
Specifies the outline size. Range: 2\-250. Default: 5.
.It Fl B Ar color | Fl \-background\-color Ar color
Specifies the background color, as \[dq]#RRGGBB\[dq] in hexadecimal (e.g. \[dq]#02266b\[dq] for dark blue) or name (e.g. \[dq]white\[dq]). Default: white.
.It Fl I Ar pattern | Fl \-pattern\-text Ar pattern
Specifies a pattern for the text, e.g. \[dq]Electric Blue\[dq].
The name must be a pattern in GIMP (.pat file, usually in
.Pa /usr/share/gimp/*/patterns/
or
.Pa /usr/local/share/gimp/*/patterns/ ).
The available patterns can be listed with
.Xr gs\-list\-patterns 1.
Default: Electric Blue.
.Pp
Note: The usage of the pattern still needs to be enabled by
.Fl \-use\-pattern\-text Cm on Ns !
.It Fl i Ar on|off | Fl \-use\-pattern\-text Ar on|off
Turns usage of a pattern for the text on or off. Default: off.
.It Fl J Ar pattern | Fl \-pattern\-outline Ar pattern
Specifies a pattern for the outline, e.g. \[dq]Electric Blue\[dq].
The name must be a pattern in GIMP (.pat file, usually in
.Pa /usr/share/gimp/*/patterns/
or
.Pa /usr/local/share/gimp/*/patterns/ ).
The available patterns can be listed with
.Xr gs\-list\-patterns 1.
Default: Electric Blue.
.Pp
Note: The usage of the pattern still needs to be enabled by
.Fl \-use\-pattern\-outline Cm on Ns !
.It Fl j Ar on|off | Fl \-use\-pattern\-outline Ar on|off
Turns usage of a pattern for the outline on or off. Default: off.
.It Fl R Ar pattern | Fl \-pattern\-overlay Ar pattern
Specifies a pattern for the overlay, e.g. \[dq]Parque #1\[dq].
The name must be a pattern in GIMP (.pat file, usually in
.Pa /usr/share/gimp/*/patterns/
or
.Pa /usr/local/share/gimp/*/patterns/ ).
The available patterns can be listed with
.Xr gs\-list\-patterns 1.
Default: Parque #1.
.Pp
Note: The usage of the pattern still needs to be enabled by
.Fl \-use\-pattern\-overlay Cm on Ns !
.It Fl r Ar on|off | Fl \-use\-pattern\-overlay Ar on|off
Turns usage of a pattern for the overlay on or off. Default: off.
.It Fl s Ar on|off | Fl \-use\-shadow Ar on|off
Turns usage of shadow on or off. Default: on.
.It Fl X Ar offset | Fl \-shadow\-offset\-x Ar offset
Sets the x\-offset for the shadow. Range: 0\-100. Default: 8.
.It Fl Y Ar offset | Fl \-shadow\-offset\-y Ar offset
Sets the y\-offset for the shadow. Range: 0\-100. Default: 8.
.It Fl q | Fl \-quiet
Quiet mode: suppress GIMP console output. This is the default.
.It Fl w | Fl \-verbose
Verbose mode: print GIMP console output and processing details.
.It Fl h | Fl \-help
Prints the program's command\-line parameters and exits.
.It Fl v | Fl \-version
Prints the program version and exits.
.El
.\" ###### Exit status ######################################################
.Sh EXIT STATUS
The
.Nm
tool exits with 0 on success, and >0 in case of an error.
.\" ###### Examples #########################################################
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bl -bullet
.It
gs\-glossytext NorNet1.png \[dq]NorNet Testbed\[dq] \-\-font\-name \[dq]Noto Sans Bold\[dq] \-\-font\-size 128 \-\-outline\-size 5
.It
gs\-glossytext NorNet2.png \[dq]NorNet Testbed\[dq] \-\-font\-name \[dq]Comic Sans MS Bold\[dq] \-\-font\-size 256 \-\-outline\-size 32
.It
gs\-glossytext NorNet3.png \[dq]NorNet Testbed\[dq] \-\-font\-name \[dq]Comic Sans MS Bold\[dq] \-\-font\-size 256 \-\-outline\-size 32 \-\-blend\-gradient\-text \[dq]Brushed Aluminium\[dq] \-\-blend\-gradient\-outline \[dq]Golden\[dq]
.It
gs\-glossytext Test1.png \[dq]Test\[dq] \-\-font\-size 256 \-\-outline\-size 32 \-\-blend\-gradient\-text \[dq]Land 1\[dq] \-\-pattern\-outline \[dq]Marble #3\[dq] \-\-use\-pattern\-outline on
.It
gs\-glossytext Test2.png \[dq]Test\[dq] \-\-font\-size 256 \-\-outline\-size 16 \-I \[dq]Marble #1\[dq] \-i on \-J \[dq]Marble #2\[dq] \-j on
.It
gs\-glossytext Test3.png \[dq]Test\[dq] \-\-font\-size 256 \-\-outline\-size 16 \-G \[dq]Yellow Orange\[dq] \-L \[dq]Cold Steel\[dq]
.It
gs\-glossytext Test4.png \[dq]Generated on $(date \-R)\[dq] \-F \[dq]Open Sans Bold\[dq] \-S 64 \-\-use\-shadow off
.It
gs\-glossytext M2EC.webp \[dq]M²EC 2026\[dq] \-\-font\-name \[dq]Lobster Two Bold Italic\[dq] \-\-font\-size 128 \-\-outline\-size 12
.It
gs\-glossytext Chinese.png \[dq]托马斯博士\[dq] \-F \[dq]Noto Sans Bold\[dq] \-S 256 \-O 24
.It
gs\-glossytext \-\-help
.It
gs\-glossytext \-h
.It
gs\-glossytext \-\-version
.It
gs\-glossytext \-v
.El
